{#- =========================================================================
    Shared UI macros. Import with:
      {% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}

    ── THE PAGE HERO — one component for EVERY page, the home page included ──
    ui.pageHero(lang, title, subtitle="", icon="", eyebrow="", opts=null)
      Renders <section class="gv-hero page-hero" data-gv-hero>: the committee's animated
      grapevine art (hero-canvas.js — base.njk loads it on every page, no pageScripts entry
      needed) over the navy → NETA-blue gradient, fading into the page at the bottom.
      SAME HEIGHT on every page, counting the fixed 64px header that sits on top of it:
        ≥1024px: 30rem (480px) · 768–1023px: 28rem (448px) · phones: 24rem (384px) minimum.
      The content starts at the same height on every page (pinned under the header, not
      centered), so the title never jumps between pages; a shorter hero shows more art below
      its text. The hero only grows when its content does not fit (desktop: 312px of room),
      so keep it short: eyebrow (a few words) · title · subtitle (1–2 lines on desktop) ·
      ONE actions row · optional compact stats (up to 4 short numbers).
      Contract: eyebrow "<Area> · <topic>" (a label, never a status) · title ≤ 2 lines on a 390px
      phone · subtitle ≤ 110 characters EN / 135 ES · actions: exactly one btn-light first (the
      page's main task) + at most 2 btn-on-dark; phones show at most 2 (max-md:hidden on the 3rd);
      no jump buttons when the page has a ui.pageNav · stats are hidden below 768px.
      An empty call body or aside slot renders nothing (no empty div, no empty right column).
      Anything bigger — search boxes, filters, long stat rows, countdown cards — goes in the
      first block BELOW the hero (see "Page start").

      Plain:
        {{ ui.pageHero(lang, "nav.events" | t(lang), "committee.events.hero_sub" | t(lang), "calendar-days", "committee.events.eyebrow" | t(lang)) }}
      With one actions row and compact stats (children of the body are spaced 1.25rem apart):
        {% call ui.pageHero(lang, title, subtitle, "library", eyebrow) %}
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn-light" href="…">…</a>
            <a class="btn-on-dark" href="…">…</a>
          </div>
          {{ ui.heroStats([{ value: 56, label: "stories" }, { value: 12, label: "episodes" }]) }}
        {% endcall %}
      opts (all optional), e.g. { id: "homeHero", titleId: "home-title", aside: true }:
        id           id of the <section>
        titleId      id of the <h1>; the section is then labelled by it (a named region)
        eyebrowIcon  icon name shown in the eyebrow pill (e.g. "grapes")
        class        extra classes for the <section>
        aside        true → two columns from 1024px: the call body's "aside" slot goes on the
                     right (the home page's meeting card). Use a call block with a slot argument:
          {% call(slot) ui.pageHero(L, title, lead, "", eyebrow, { id: "homeHero", titleId: "home-title", aside: true }) %}
            {%- if slot == "aside" %}<aside class="…">…</aside>
            {%- else %}<div class="hero-actions">…</div>{% endif %}
          {% endcall %}
                     Below 1024px the aside stacks under the copy and makes the hero taller —
                     hide or shorten it there (e.g. class="max-lg:hidden").
      title may be trusted HTML marked | safe ("home.hero_title" | t(L) | mdInline | safe);
      *emphasis* in it shows in warm gold italics. subtitle is printed with | safe, so pass
      i18n strings only — never synced third-party text.

    ── Page start — the first block after the hero, use exactly ONE of: ──
      page-overlap  a card, search box or sub-nav that tucks into the hero's faded bottom edge:
                      <section class="container-page page-overlap"><div class="card card-pad">…
                    (it overlaps the fade by 1.5rem on phones / 2.5rem from 640px — never the text)
      page-start    a normal section, used INSTEAD of "section" (it keeps the bottom padding):
                      <section class="container-page page-start">…
    ── Width (main.css) ──
      container-page  full width up to 1920px; side padding var(--gutter) (16px → 72px).
      grid-cards / grid-cards-fit   card grids: 1 → 2 → 3 (1024px) → 4 (1536px) → 5 (1800px) columns.
      grid-cards-4   short lists of link cards: 2 → 3 → 4 (1280px) → 5 (1800px), stretched to fill.
                     All grids drop columns rather than squeeze cards (next to a sidebar, say);
                     override per grid with [--cards-max:N] / [--cards-min:15rem].
      rail + rail-item   scroll-snap rows showing more items per view on wide screens ([--rail-n:N]).
      measure (72ch) · layout-aside (main + right sidebar) · layout-sidebar (left filters + results).
      sticky-aside / sticky-aside-xl   the ONLY sticky side column (from 1024 / 1280px, windows ≥ 640px
                     tall, never taller than the window). Nothing else sticks (main.css "Sticky rules").
    ── Small components (main.css) ──
      chip-row (scrolls on phones, wraps from 1024) · chip-row-nowrap (never wraps) · meta-row
      (date · show · time, dots drawn by CSS) · card-h (panel title with icon) · step-num (28px
      numbered circle) · panel-muted (flat note panel) · section-band (tinted full-width band, with
      "section") · tap-link (44px standalone link on touch) · btn-sm and chip are 44px on phones.

    ── Section header — ui.sectionHead(title, subtitle="", href="", linkLabel="", icon="", opts=null) ──
      Eyebrow form (use it for every top-level section):
        {{ ui.sectionHead("Upcoming events", "Workshops, booths and assemblies near you.", "/events/" | lurl(lang),
             "common.view_all" | t(lang), "calendar-days",
             { eyebrow: "Committee", tone: "text-vine", id: "events-title", lang: lang }) }}
      opts: eyebrow (turns the eyebrow form on) · tone (a LITERAL class: text-gv default, text-lv,
            text-grape, text-vine) · id (on the h2) · level: 3 (h3 instead of h2) · class (extra
            classes on the wrapper) · lang (ALWAYS pass it: the external-link text needs it).
      href + linkLabel → the right-hand "all" link (btn-secondary btn-sm + arrow). A call body adds
      one more action in that slot, before the "all" link:
        {% call ui.sectionHead(title, sub, href, label, "headphones", { eyebrow: "Media", tone: "text-grape", lang: lang }) %}
          <button class="btn-ghost btn-sm" type="button">…</button>
        {% endcall %}
      Without opts.eyebrow it renders the legacy form (icon inside the h2) — migrate those callers.

    ── In-page nav — ui.pageNav(items, lang, opts=null) — long pages only (5+ sections) ──
        <div class="container-page page-overlap">{{ ui.pageNav([
          { href: "#botm", label: "Book of the Month", icon: "book-open" },
          { href: "#magazines", label: "Magazines" } ], lang) }}</div>
      A card: "On this page" (from 1280px) + one row of chips that never wraps. opts: label, class.

    ── Freshness — ui.freshness(date, lang, opts=null) — at most once per page, next to its list ──
        {{ ui.freshness(site.built, lang) }}                  → "Updated 2 hours ago"
        {{ ui.freshness(site.built, lang, { note: true }) }}  → "… · We keep it updated regularly"
        {{ ui.freshness(null, lang, { note: true }) }}        → "We keep it updated regularly"

    ── Next steps — ui.nextSteps(items, lang) — the closing block; up to 4 link cards ──
        {{ ui.sectionHead(…, "", "", "", "compass", { eyebrow: "common.next_steps" | t(lang), lang: lang }) }}
        {{ ui.nextSteps([{ href: "/shop/" | lurl(lang), title: "Subscribe", text: "Print or digital.",
             cta: "See prices", icon: "shopping-bag", tone: "lv" }, …], lang) }}
      Never repeat a link the page already gave as its main action, nor the footer lists.

    ── For committee members — ui.memberHelp(lang, summary, opts=null) — collapsed disclosure ──
        {% call ui.memberHelp(lang, "How to add documents", { id: "members" }) %}…how-to…{% endcall %}
      Committee-only how-tos (Drive folders, access, posting) go here, just before the closing block.
    ========================================================================= -#}

{% macro pageHero(lang, title, subtitle="", icon="", eyebrow="", opts=null) %}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}
{#- caller() returns a SafeString object, which is truthy even when it is empty, so the
    checks below test | length (0 for an empty body / aside) instead of truthiness. -#}
{%- set heroBody = (caller() | trim) if caller else "" -%}
{%- set heroAside = (caller("aside") | trim) if (caller and o.aside) else "" -%}
{%- set hasBody = (heroBody | length) > 0 -%}
{%- set hasAside = (heroAside | length) > 0 -%}
<section class="gv-hero page-hero{{ ' gv-hero--split' if hasAside }}{{ (' ' ~ o.class) if o.class }}" data-gv-hero{% if o.id %} id="{{ o.id }}"{% endif %}{% if o.titleId %} aria-labelledby="{{ o.titleId }}"{% endif %}>
  <canvas class="gv-hero-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="gv-hero-inner container-page">
    <div class="gv-hero-copy">
      {% if eyebrow %}<p class="gv-hero-eyebrow">{% if o.eyebrowIcon %}{% icon o.eyebrowIcon, "size-4 shrink-0" %}{% endif %}<span>{{ eyebrow }}</span></p>{% endif %}
      <h1 class="gv-hero-title"{% if o.titleId %} id="{{ o.titleId }}"{% endif %}>
        {%- if icon %}<span class="gv-hero-icon">{% icon icon, "size-6" %}</span>{% endif -%}
        <span>{{ title }}</span>
      </h1>
      {% if subtitle %}<p class="gv-hero-sub">{{ subtitle | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if hasBody %}<div class="gv-hero-body">{{ heroBody }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if hasAside %}<div class="gv-hero-aside">{{ heroAside }}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endmacro %}

{#- Compact stat row for inside pageHero's call body: display-serif number over a short label —
    the one hero-stat design for every page. stats = [{ value: 56, label: "stories" }, …]
    (or [[56, "stories"], …]); entries without a value are skipped. Shown from 768px (hidden on
    phones by the hero-stats utility — no max-sm/max-md wrapper needed); keep ≤ 4 short numbers,
    each shown only here on the page. Longer stat rows belong below the hero. -#}
{% macro heroStats(stats) %}
<dl class="hero-stats">
  {%- for s in stats %}
  {%- set v = s.value if (s.value is defined) else s[0] -%}
  {%- set l = s.label if (s.label is defined) else s[1] -%}
  {%- if v is defined and v !== null and v !== "" %}
  <div class="hero-stat"><dt>{{ l }}</dt><dd>{{ v }}</dd></div>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</dl>
{% endmacro %}

{#- Section heading — the ONE header for every top-level section (see the doc block at the top).
    Eyebrow form (opts.eyebrow): [icon] EYEBROW in the tone colour · h2 · one-line intro, with the
    "all" link (href + linkLabel) as a right-hand btn-secondary btn-sm with a trailing arrow, and
    an optional extra action from the call body. The legacy form (no opts.eyebrow) keeps the
    icon inside the h2 — migrate those callers to the eyebrow form. -#}
{% macro sectionHead(title, subtitle="", href="", linkLabel="", icon="", opts=null) %}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}
{%- set tag = "h3" if o.level == 3 else "h2" -%}
{%- set extra = (caller() | trim) if caller else "" -%}
{%- set ext = href and href.startsWith("http") -%}
<div class="section-head{{ (' ' ~ o.class) if o.class }}">
  <div class="min-w-0 max-w-3xl">
    {%- if o.eyebrow %}
    <p class="eyebrow flex items-center gap-2 {{ o.tone or 'text-gv' }}">{% if icon %}{% icon icon, "size-4 shrink-0" %}{% endif %}<span>{{ o.eyebrow }}</span></p>
    <{{ tag }}{% if o.id %} id="{{ o.id }}"{% endif %} class="h-section mt-2 text-balance">{{ title }}</{{ tag }}>
    {%- else %}
    <{{ tag }}{% if o.id %} id="{{ o.id }}"{% endif %} class="h-section flex items-center gap-2.5">{% if icon %}<span class="text-gv">{% icon icon, "size-6" %}</span>{% endif %}{{ title }}</{{ tag }}>
    {%- endif %}
    {% if subtitle %}<p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ subtitle | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {%- if href or (extra | length) %}
  <div class="section-head-actions">{{ extra }}
    {%- if href %}<a href="{{ href }}" class="btn-secondary btn-sm"{% if ext %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ linkLabel }} {% icon "arrow-right", "size-4" %}{% if ext %}<span class="sr-only"> ({{ 'common.external' | t(o.lang or 'en') }})</span>{% endif %}</a>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{#- In-page navigation for long pages: <div class="container-page page-overlap">{{ ui.pageNav(items, lang) }}</div>
    items = [{ href: "#botm", label: "Book of the Month", icon: "book-open" }, …] (icon optional;
    items without an href are skipped). opts: { label, class }. Never sticky. -#}
{% macro pageNav(items, lang, opts=null) %}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}{%- set lbl = o.label or ("common.on_this_page" | t(lang)) -%}
<nav class="page-nav card{{ (' ' ~ o.class) if o.class }}" aria-label="{{ lbl }}">
  <p class="page-nav-label" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "list", "size-4 shrink-0" %} {{ lbl }}</p>
  <ul class="chip-row-nowrap" role="list">
    {%- for it in items %}{% if it.href %}
    <li><a class="chip" href="{{ it.href }}">{% if it.icon %}{% icon it.icon, "size-4 shrink-0" %}{% endif %}{{ it.label }}</a></li>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</nav>
{% endmacro %}

{#- How fresh a list is — the ONLY way to say it, at most once per page, next to the list it
    describes: "Updated 2 hours ago" (app.js turns time[data-relative] into relative time; without
    JS it shows the date). opts: { note: true } adds "· We keep it updated regularly"; class.
    With no date and note: true it says only "We keep it updated regularly". -#}
{% macro freshness(date, lang, opts=null) %}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}
{%- if date %}<p class="freshness{{ (' ' ~ o.class) if o.class }}">{% icon "refresh-cw", "size-3.5 shrink-0" %}<span>{{ "common.updated" | t(lang) }} <time datetime="{{ date | isoDate }}" data-relative>{{ date | fmtDate(lang, "medium") }}</time>{% if o.note %} · {{ "common.kept_updated" | t(lang) }}{% endif %}</span></p>
{%- elif o.note %}<p class="freshness{{ (' ' ~ o.class) if o.class }}">{% icon "refresh-cw", "size-3.5 shrink-0" %}<span>{{ "common.kept_updated" | t(lang) }}</span></p>{% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Closing "Next steps": up to 4 link cards (grid only — put ui.sectionHead above it).
    items = [{ href, title, text, cta, icon, tone: "gv"|"lv"|"grape"|"vine" }, …]
    The whole card is the link; cta is a specific verb ("Subscribe", never "Open"). -#}
{% macro nextSteps(items, lang) %}
{%- set tones = { gv: "bg-gv-soft text-gv", lv: "bg-lv-soft text-lv", grape: "bg-grape-soft text-grape", vine: "bg-vine-soft text-vine" } -%}
<ul class="grid-cards-4" role="list">
  {%- for it in items %}{% if loop.index <= 4 and it.href %}{%- set ext = it.href.startsWith("http") -%}{%- set ic = it.icon or "arrow-right" -%}
  <li class="card card-link relative flex flex-col gap-3 p-5">
    <span class="grid size-11 place-items-center rounded-xl {{ tones[it.tone or 'gv'] or tones.gv }}">{% icon ic, "size-5" %}</span>
    <h3 class="h-card"><a class="no-underline after:absolute after:inset-0 after:rounded-[var(--radius-card)] hover:text-gv" href="{{ it.href }}"{% if ext %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ it.title }}{% if ext %}<span class="sr-only"> ({{ 'common.external' | t(lang) }})</span>{% endif %}</a></h3>
    {% if it.text %}<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ it.text }}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if it.cta %}<span class="mt-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 pt-1 text-sm font-semibold text-gv" aria-hidden="true">{{ it.cta }} {% icon "arrow-right", "size-4" %}</span>{% endif %}
  </li>
  {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endmacro %}

{#- "For committee members" — a collapsed disclosure for committee-only how-tos (Drive folders,
    access, posting). Goes just before the page's closing block. The call body is the content:
      {% call ui.memberHelp(lang, "How to add documents", { id: "members" }) %}<ol>…</ol>{% endcall %} -#}
{% macro memberHelp(lang, summary, opts=null) %}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}
<details class="card group{{ (' ' ~ o.class) if o.class }}"{% if o.id %} id="{{ o.id }}"{% endif %}>
  <summary class="flex min-h-14 cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-3 rounded-[var(--radius-card)] px-5 py-3 sm:px-6 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
    <span class="grid size-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-vine-soft text-vine">{% icon "key-round", "size-5" %}</span>
    <span class="min-w-0 flex-1"><span class="eyebrow block">{{ "common.for_members" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="block font-semibold text-ink">{{ summary }}</span></span>
    {% icon "chevron-down", "size-5 shrink-0 text-muted transition group-open:rotate-180" %}
  </summary>
  <div class="border-t border-line px-5 py-5 sm:px-6">{{ caller() if caller }}</div>
</details>
{% endmacro %}

{#- Empty state box -#}
{% macro emptyState(icon, title, text="", ctaHref="", ctaLabel="") %}
<div class="empty-state">
  <span class="mx-auto mb-3 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-surface-2 text-faint">{% icon icon, "size-6" %}</span>
  <p class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ title }}</p>
  {% if text %}<p class="mx-auto mt-1 max-w-md text-sm">{{ text | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if ctaHref %}<a class="btn-secondary btn-sm mt-4" href="{{ ctaHref }}"{% if ctaHref.startsWith('http') %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ ctaLabel }}</a>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{#- Source label + color for any item -#}
{% macro sourceBadge(item, lang) %}
{%- set src = item.source -%}
{%- set refHost = (item.extra.referrers[0].url | hostname) if (item.extra and item.extra.external and item.extra.referrers and item.extra.referrers.length) else "" -%}
{%- set isLv = ('lavina' in refHost) if refHost else (item.extra and item.extra.host and 'lavina' in item.extra.host) -%}
{%- if src == "podcast" %}<span class="badge-grape">{% icon "headphones", "size-3" %} {{ "kind.episode" | t(lang) }}</span>
{%- elif src == "youtube" %}<span class="badge-grape">{% icon "youtube", "size-3" %} YouTube</span>
{%- elif src == "instagram" %}<span class="badge-grape">{% icon "instagram", "size-3" %} Instagram</span>
{%- elif src == "drive" or src == "committee" %}<span class="badge-vine">{% icon "users", "size-3" %} NETA 65</span>
{%- elif src == "crawl" %}<span class="{{ 'badge-lv' if isLv else 'badge-gv' }}">{% icon "file-text", "size-3" %} {{ "La Viña" if isLv else "Grapevine" }}</span>
{%- elif src == "lavina" or item.category == "lv" or item.category == "lv-calendar" %}<span class="badge-lv">{% icon "grapes", "size-3" %} La Viña</span>
{%- elif src == "grapevine" or item.category == "gv" or item.category == "gv-calendar" %}<span class="badge-gv">{% icon "grapes", "size-3" %} Grapevine</span>
{%- else %}<span class="badge-muted">{{ src }}</span>{%- endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Small "auto-translated" note when this language version is machine translated -#}
{% macro autoNote(item, lang) %}
{%- if item | machineFor(lang) %}<span class="auto-note" title="{{ 'common.auto_translated_help' | t(lang) }}">{% icon "languages", "size-3" %} {{ "common.auto_translated" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{#- "Details to be confirmed": an event whose date, place or times are not final yet (content/events
    `tentative: true`, or STATUS:TENTATIVE in an outside calendar). The explanation is the tooltip and,
    for screen readers, part of the badge itself (a tooltip alone never reaches touch or keyboard users). -#}
{% macro tentativeBadge(lang) %}
<span class="badge-tbc" title="{{ 'committee.events.tentative_help' | t(lang) }}">{% icon "calendar-clock", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.events.tentative" | t(lang) }}<span class="sr-only">: {{ "committee.events.tentative_help" | t(lang) }}</span></span>
{%- endmacro %}

{#- Language pill (shows the ORIGINAL language of content when it differs from the page) -#}
{% macro langPill(item, lang) %}
{%- if item.lang and item.lang != lang and item.lang != "und" %}<span class="badge-muted uppercase" title="{{ ('lang.' + item.lang) | t(lang) }}">{{ item.lang }}</span>{% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Generic content card for any Item (article, pdf, video, episode, post, drive doc, announcement). -#}
{% macro itemCard(item, lang, showImage=true) %}
{%- set title = item | tx("title", lang) -%}
{%- set summary = item | tx("summary", lang) -%}
{%- set href = item.url | lurl(lang) -%}
{%- set external = href and (href.startsWith("http")) -%}
<article class="card card-link group relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden">
  {% if showImage and item.image %}
  <div class="card-media {{ 'aspect-square' if item.kind == 'post' else '' }}">
    <img src="{{ item.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">
    {% if item.kind == "video" or item.kind == "episode" %}<span class="absolute inset-0 grid place-items-center"><span class="grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-black/55 text-white backdrop-blur transition group-hover:scale-110">{% icon "play", "size-5 translate-x-px" %}</span></span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-2 p-5">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
      {{ sourceBadge(item, lang) }}
      {% if item.is_new %}<span class="badge-new">{{ "common.new" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
      {{ langPill(item, lang) }}
    </div>
    <h3 class="h-card">
      <a href="{{ href }}" class="no-underline after:absolute after:inset-0 hover:text-gv"{% if external %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ title }}</a>
    </h3>
    {% if summary %}<p class="line-clamp-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ summary | excerpt(200) }}</p>{% endif %}
    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 pt-2 text-xs text-faint">
      {% if item.date %}<time datetime="{{ item.date | isoDate }}">{{ item.date | fmtDate(lang, "medium") }}</time>{% else %}<span></span>{% endif %}
      {{ autoNote(item, lang) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
{% endmacro %}
